randomness for the tested feature at the available draw counts. WARN results are a signal to review that specific test/pool (often due to low p-values or notable deviations), but they are not
proof of bias or predictability. INSUFFICIENT_DATA results mean the test’s assumptions are not met (e.g., very small expected bucket counts in gaps/triples), so the p-value and chi-square 
should not be used for strong conclusions. NOT_APPLICABLE indicates a test wasn’t meaningfully run for that game/pool configuration. None of these historical audits identify or predict future
winning numbers.
